# Agent Autonomy

This repo is operated entirely by the agent. The user sets vision; the agent executes.

## Rules

1. Run `yarn verify` (or `scripts/verify.sh`) before declaring done
2. Run `yarn check:requirements` when blocked on deploy, secrets, Supabase, Vercel, or e2e
3. Use **MCP plugins first**, then CLIs (`supabase`, `vercel`, `gh`, `yarn`) — not service dashboards
4. **Create and configure cloud resources yourself** (Supabase projects, migrations, auth, Vercel env, GitHub secrets) — see [`.cursor/rules/mcp-first-ops.mdc`](mcp-first-ops.mdc). For local GitHub (push/PR/secrets): **`gh` CLI auth only** — never the project `.env.local` `GITHUB_TOKEN` (Issues PAT; poisons `gh` via env).
5. Pause only at documented user gates in `docs/prerequisites.md` — never for tasks you have tools to perform
6. Self-fix CI failures; never ask the user to triage logs
7. Propagate secrets from `.env.local` via CLI — user does not configure GitHub/Vercel manually
8. If MCP `serverStatus` is `needsAuth`, call `mcp_auth` and retry before asking the user
9. **UI copy / a11y / dialog title changes → update `tests/e2e` (and Maestro) in the same change** — see [`.cursor/rules/playwright-chrome.mdc`](playwright-chrome.mdc). Do not wait for CI to discover broken `getByRole` names.
10. **Bug fixes → update rules/docs in the same change** — classify the bug, add a prevention delta to the relevant `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` or `docs/`, and add e2e when reproducible. See [`.cursor/rules/wrap-up-learning.mdc`](wrap-up-learning.mdc). A fix without a rules update does not complete the task.
11. **`user-suggestion` GitHub issues → Export JSON + SuperAdmin comments first** — do not implement from the issue body alone; propose approach pivots on the thread. See [`.cursor/rules/user-suggestion-issues.mdc`](user-suggestion-issues.mdc).

## Definition of done

- Features / refactors: `yarn verify` passes; learnings captured when non-obvious ([wrap-up-learning](wrap-up-learning.mdc)).
- **Bug fixes:** code + test (when feasible) + **prevention rule in the same PR** + `yarn verify`.

- **Accounts exist** — GitHub, Supabase, Vercel (ownership/billing; one-time signup)
- **Access tokens in `.env.local`** — `SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN`, `VERCEL_TOKEN` (only if MCP auth cannot complete)
- **Product choices** — when genuinely ambiguous (e.g. custom domain name)

**Not user gates:** creating Supabase projects, applying migrations, auth redirect URLs, fetching API keys, syncing Vercel env, setting GitHub secrets, deploying.
